  "hqOverride": true,
  "notes": {
    "answered": [
      "States are skippable by role, and role determines the path.",
      "Writer tiers are UltraDTP, MidDTP, SWUser and AI-assist. All apply to every state up to Grammarly Edit Complete — no tier skips that state. 1Editor is not a tier: it is a property a writer carries on top of one, so someone can be MidDTP and 1Editor, or SWUser and 1Editor.",
      "At Grammarly Edit Complete, self-publishing is decided by the tier × article-type matrix — not by tier alone. The same writer's News brief and Shorty can take different paths.",
      "Access is three-way, not two. A tier either self-publishes a type, writes it and sends it to review, or has no access and never authors it at all. Only the middle case reaches the copy edit states.",
      "Editors per article comes from three things: the tier's access to the type, whether the writer carries 1Editor, and nothing else. Anything self-published gets none. Anything else gets a copyeditor, then a financial editor — unless the writer is 1Editor, in which case the copyeditor finishes it.",
      "Most articles are published or scheduled straight out of In Financial Edit — the FFE finishes there. Edits Done is not a step on that path.",
      "In Copy Edit is a branch point, and 1Editor is what decides it. A standard writer's article goes on to financial edit; a 1Editor writer's article is published or scheduled by the copyeditor from In Copy Edit. UltraDTP, MidDTP and SWUser can carry 1Editor; AI-assist cannot.",
      "No tier skips copy edit but still needs FFE — financial edit always follows copy edit.",
      "Send-backs land in Edits Required, from either In Copy Edit or In Financial Edit — never back to Compose.",
      "Edits Done is optional. An article only reaches it after a send-back: In Copy Edit or In Financial Edit returns it to Edits Required, the writer resubmits, and it lands in Edits Done. An article that is never sent back never touches it.",
      "Nothing publishes from Edits Required. Once the writer resubmits, the article moves to Edits Done — where it goes back to the FFE, or is published or scheduled there by an FFE or, for a 1Editor writer's article, a copyeditor.",
      "HQ editors can move an article from any state to any other."
    ],
    "open": [
      "Edits Done — claimed by one owner, or an open queue? Unclear whether it stays claimed by the FFE who finished the edit, or reopens for anyone eligible to pick up. Two things narrow this: it only ever affects articles that were sent back, since Edits Done is unreachable otherwise; and whoever holds it can publish or schedule, so the answer decides who is allowed to finish a resubmitted article.",
      "Published — access undecided. Nothing holds a published article; it lands there automatically. The open question is who can get back into one: can anyone edit or re-schedule it in place, or is HQ unpublish-then-republish the only route? Carried over from the source diagram, which badged Published as undecided without writing up what was undecided.",
      "Unpublished: leaning HQ and superusers only, since they are the only ones who can send an article there — but that could become a bottleneck. Not needed to start the build."
    ],
    "routing": "Copy edit and financial edit are claim-based, so each queue needs a defined list of eligible claimants — by group if Sanity supports it, otherwise by individual. Articles that fail the self-publish matrix route to a copyeditor, and every article goes on to a financial editor unless its writer carries 1Editor — so the size of the FFE queue depends on how many writers hold that modifier, not on which tier they are in. A new article type starts with no access for anyone, so adding one grants nobody anything until the matrix is filled in — deliberate, but it means the matrix is the gate on rolling out a new format.",
    "caveat": "HQ any-to-any and the copy-edit send-back both need non-sequential transitions, which Sanity does not support today."
  }
}